on january 1st 2021  the night county sheriff's office  rescued a kidnapping victim who had been  missing since october of  nye county sheriff's office detectives  unit began working with the las vegas  metropolitan police department missing  persons unit in october of 2020  to locate a missing adult who was  possibly kidnapped it was believed at  the time that the victim was taken to an  unknown location in pahrump by keith  holman  and kristen pfaff despite a  collaborative effort between the two  agencies the victim was not located and  the leads to the victim's location were  exhausted  on january 1st night county sheriff's  office dispatch received a phone call  from the victim's mother  she said that her daughter was messaging  her on facebook this was the first time  anyone had heard from the victim since  she went missing in las vegas in march  of 2020.  while communicating through facebook the  victim was able to describe the  residence in which she was being held  and nye county sheriff's deputies and  detectives began searching that area  detectives were eventually able to  locate the exact address and the victim  was rescued  the investigation reveals that keith  holman sexually assaulted the victim in  2018.  in march of 2020 the victim was  kidnapped by keith holman and kristen  phaf and brought to parump where she  remained concealed and confined for the  next nine months  during her confinement the victim was  forced to perform manual labor and if  she refused she was battered  the suspects frequently traveled from  las vegas to parump and would leave the  victim locked in the residence with  little food for days at a time  the building that the victim was  confined was secured with bars on the  windows and steel doors and barricades  blocking the doors  the building was surrounded by cameras  and motion detectors holmen and phaf are  wanted by the nye county sheriff's  office for the kidnapping and false  imprisonment of the victim  holmen is considered armed and dangerous  and is possibly in possession of a  handgun  you
 

